# TypeScript (Excalidraw monorepo)

Source of truth: root `tsconfig.json`, `packages/tsconfig.base.json`, `.eslintrc.json`, `AGENTS.md` (`yarn test:typecheck`, `yarn test:code`). Formatting: `@excalidraw/prettier-config` via `yarn test:other` / `yarn fix`.

## Compiler baseline

- **`strict: true`** everywhere — prefer correct types over `any`. Use unknown + narrowing at boundaries (untrusted JSON, network, storage).
- Root config also sets **`noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`** and **`forceConsistentCasingInFileNames`** — keep switches explicit and paths’ casing consistent with imports.
- **`isolatedModules: true`** (app/tsconfig) — avoid patterns that require whole-program types to emit valid JS (e.g. rely on `const enum` pitfalls carefully).

## Imports (enforced by ESLint)

- **Type-only imports:** use `import type { … }` / `import { type X }` per `@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-imports` (`fixStyle: separate-type-imports`).
- **`import/order`:** groups + blank lines; `@excalidraw/**` is treated as external after other externals — follow existing file patterns.
- **Restricted imports:**
  - Do not import **`jotai`** directly — use **`editor-jotai`** or **`app-jotai`** (see `no-restricted-imports` in `.eslintrc.json`).
  - Under **`packages/excalidraw/**`**: do not import from the **`@excalidraw/excalidraw`** barrel for value imports; use **direct relative paths** (type-only imports from the barrel are allowed).

## Types and suppressions

- Prefer **`type`** for simple object shapes; use **`interface`** when extending/merging is useful — match surrounding files.
- Avoid **`any`**. If unavoidable, keep it **local** and document why.
- Do not add broad **`@ts-ignore`**. Prefer **`@ts-expect-error`** with a **short reason** so removal breaks when the types fix the issue.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
// @ts-ignore
foo(bar);

// ✅ BETTER
// @ts-expect-error HarfBuzz WASM binding exposes non-standard `.buffer`
foo(bar);
```

## Workspace paths

- Use **`@excalidraw/*`** path aliases from `tsconfig` for packages — avoid deep fragile relative paths when a public package entry exists.

## How to verify

- From the repo root: `yarn test:typecheck` (TypeScript) and `yarn test:code` (ESLint, including import and typing rules).
- After edits: `yarn fix:code` to apply safe auto-fixes, then re-run `yarn test:code` to confirm a clean lint pass.
- Optional full gate: `yarn test:all` (see `AGENTS.md`).
